Bad example: Quote: ''POs need my sign-off'' -> purchase approval, route to purchasing_process.', '["approvals go through", "over $N needs", "I sign every check", "it''s an email chain", "no real approvals"]'::jsonb, '["''No approvals'' stated is a finding (control gap), record it. Purchase approvals (pre-spend) are purchasing_process", "this is bill/payment approval (post-invoice)."]'::jsonb, NULL, 500, true),
(NULL, 'deal', 'vendor_payment_methods', 'How are vendor bills paid today?', 'multiselect', 'Payment rails in use: check, ACH, card, wire, bill-pay platform, and rough mix.', 'Payables, Purchasing & Expenses', 'Payment rails in use: check, ACH, card, wire, bill-pay platform, and rough mix. (merged with payment_methods: one definition covers vendor payment rails)', 'List of methods + mix if stated. Platforms named (Bill.com, Melio) also write company_systems.
